  The repository follows the tam-idol 1.1.0 layout (W16). Source
  installation builds pinned clones, verifies native prerequisites and
  destination ownership, and selects the installed cultivar by digest.

  In Develop, source preflight requires the Arch Gum package and its
  native executable (W17), and tam-fleet validates source-install
  profiles from the capability catalog (W18). W23 adds the Arch ffmpeg
  prerequisite for text-console PrtSc capture.

  In Develop (W19), the 0.6.38 product fixes are ready on dev:
  - Fresh-login man-page lookup resolves cultivar and rootstock pages
    via standard man-db PATH discovery and /usr/share/man integration
    after /etc/profile unsets MANPATH.
  - tam-update reports installed foreign/local packages (pacman -Qm),
    lists pending AUR updates read-only (yay -Qua), and prints frozen-
    recipe review/build instructions.
  - tam-boot excludes intermediate kernel messages during the disk
    passphrase prompt from slow steps, bounds kernel gap analysis to
    startup completion, and sorts slow steps descending by duration.
  - tam-vt-screenshot, tamlinux-vt-prtsc.map, tamlinux-vt.vtrgb,
    kbrequest.target, tam-vt-keymap.service, and
    tam-vt-screenshot.service are packaged in the cultivar and systemd
    system unit layout.
  - tam-fleet capture reads deployed plugin manifests and active source-
    install manifests directly into state/bom.json, and tam-dev resolves
    the src/commands, src/desktop, and tests repository layout and
    /usr/lib/tamlinux/current/... runtime paths (W20).
  - Drafted arch/keybindings.md (W22) with initial first-principles notes
    for the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard across compositor,
    terminal, shell, editor, and tools.


